  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Business for Social Responisbility for MDG 5 - BSR for MDG 5</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Business for Social Responsibility f&#xf6;r att        st&#xe4;rka millenieutvecklingsm&#xe5;l 5, minskad m&#xf6;dra-   d&#xf6;dlighet</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">BSR genomf&#xf6;r en insats som syftar till att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra sexuell och reproduktiv h&#xe4;lsa hos kvinnliga fabriksarbetare som i geng&#xe4;ld minskar arbetsbortfall f&#xf6;r f&#xf6;retaget. HER arbetar med att f&#xf6;rmedla kontakt mellan f&#xf6;retag och organsiationer som ger utbildning p&#xe5; f&#xf6;retagen under arbetstid. Insatsen &#xe4;r en del av speciella satsningar f&#xf6;r att involvera f&#xf6;retag att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra SRHR bland kvinnliga fabriksanst&#xe4;llda</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Business for Social responsibility is carrying out a project called Health equals returns, HER, and is intended to catalyze partnerships between the private sector and local NGOs to promote female factory workes sexual and reporoductive health and rights through workplace training programes. It is a part of Swedish Special efforts and a pilot to introduce SRHR in corporate social responsibility.</narrative>
  </description>
